Removing the `envelope.status !== DocumentStatus.PENDING` guard at lines 108–110 lets execution proceed past that point for envelopes in any other status, but reaching the write transaction still requires passing every subsequent guard in the function body.

```
108:110:packages/lib/server-only/field/sign-field-with-token.ts
  if (envelope.status !== DocumentStatus.PENDING) {
    throw new Error(`Document ${envelope.id} must be pending for signing`);
  }
```

**Verified call paths and conditions**

**`field-router/router.ts`** calls `signFieldWithToken` at lines 615–633 using `procedure` (not `authenticatedProcedure`). The opened body has no envelope status pre-check. `userId` is passed as `ctx.user?.id` — optionally undefined. The `procedure` middleware's implementation is not opened, so its own access enforcement is unverified.

```
615:633:packages/trpc/server/field-router/router.ts
  signFieldWithToken: procedure.input(ZSignFieldWithTokenMutationSchema).mutation(async ({ input, ctx }) => {
    const { token, fieldId, value, isBase64, authOptions } = input;

    ctx.logger.info({
      input: {
        fieldId,
      },
    });

    return await signFieldWithToken({
      token,
      fieldId,
      value: value ?? '',
      isBase64,
      userId: ctx.user?.id,
      authOptions,
      requestMetadata: ctx.metadata.requestMetadata,
    });
  }),
```

**`apply-multi-sign-signature.ts`** pre-call rejects if any recipient's `readStatus !== ReadStatus.OPENED` (line 35), or if `recipientAccessAuthRequired || recipientActionAuthRequired` (line 52). It skips recipients where `signingStatus === SigningStatus.REJECTED` (line 61) and queries only `inserted: false, type: FieldType.SIGNATURE` fields (lines 65–72). It passes no `userId` or `authOptions` to `signFieldWithToken` (lines 76–82). `getDocumentByToken` (line 25) is called but its body is not opened — any status filtering it performs is unverified. Critically, the catch block at lines 89–97 catches any non-`AppError` throw — including the plain `Error` objects `signFieldWithToken` emits — and rethrows as `AppErrorCode.UNKNOWN_ERROR`, discarding the original message.

```
89:97:packages/trpc/server/embedding-router/apply-multi-sign-signature.ts
    } catch (error) {
      if (error instanceof AppError) {
        throw error;
      }

      throw new AppError(AppErrorCode.UNKNOWN_ERROR, {
        message: 'Failed to apply multi-sign signature',
      });
    }
```

**Remaining guards after the changed predicate** — passing line 110 does not reach the write directly. These apply in order: `assertRecipientNotExpired(recipient)` (line 112, implementation unverified); `signingStatus === SigningStatus.SIGNED` on both `recipient` and `field.recipient` → throws (line 114); `field.inserted` → throws (line 118); per-type validation for NUMBER/TEXT/CHECKBOX/RADIO/DROPDOWN (lines 127–172); `validateFieldAuth(...)` (line 174, implementation unverified); signature completeness checks (lines 203–208); `readOnly` default-value check (lines 211–231). If all pass, the transaction runs: `tx.field.update` sets `inserted: true` unconditionally (lines 237–245); `tx.signature.upsert` runs only when `isSignatureField` is true, creating a new row or updating `signatureImageAsBase64`/`typedSignature` on the existing one (lines 248–262); `tx.documentAuditLog.create` always runs (line 270).

```
247:262:packages/lib/server-only/field/sign-field-with-token.ts
    if (isSignatureField) {
      const signature = await tx.signature.upsert({
        where: {
          fieldId: field.id,
        },
        create: {
          fieldId: field.id,
          recipientId: field.recipientId,
          signatureImageAsBase64: signatureImageAsBase64,
          typedSignature: typedSignature,
        },
        update: {
          signatureImageAsBase64: signatureImageAsBase64,
          typedSignature: typedSignature,
        },
      });
```

**Pre-ship verification**

- **Statuses now permitted:** The opened body only references `DocumentStatus.PENDING`; the full `DocumentStatus` enum is not shown. Enumerate every status value that should reach the write and confirm each is intentional — the opened bodies do not establish which other status values exist.
- **`getDocumentByToken` status filtering:** Its body is not opened. Verify whether it already gates on `PENDING`; if it does, the `apply-multi-sign-signature` flow may remain protected by that helper even after your change.
- **`assertRecipientNotExpired` and `validateFieldAuth` contracts:** Neither implementation is opened. Confirm neither assumes `DocumentStatus.PENDING` as a precondition — especially `validateFieldAuth`, which receives `userId: undefined` and `authOptions: undefined` from the multi-sign caller since those fields are not forwarded there.
- **`field.inserted` invariant per status:** For the signature upsert to execute, `field.inserted` must be `false` (enforced by line 118). Verify that for whichever non-PENDING statuses you intend to allow, unsigned fields with `inserted: false` can legitimately exist, so the upsert path is reachable as intended.

The opened dependents do not prove complete coverage; `procedure` middleware, `getDocumentByToken`, `assertRecipientNotExpired`, and `validateFieldAuth` implementations remain unread.
